# Name of benchmark/experiment: FILLET Experiment 1 (warm start)
# Code: AVALON (Albedo-feedback Variable Axial-tilt Latitudinal Outgoing-Net EBM)
# Case number: 17
# Instellation (S_earth): 0.825000
# XCO2 (ppm): 280
# Obliquity (degrees): 70.00
# Mode: seasonal (limit cycle; values are means over the final orbit)
# Orbital period (days): 365.0000; steps per orbit: 365 (dt = 1.0000 days); grid: 90 equal-area cells in sin(lat), cell-centered, no node on the poles
# Albedo land/ocean/ice: 0.3000/0.2000/0.6000; heat capacity land/ocean/ice: 1e+07/4e+08/1e+07 J m^-2 K^-1; D = 0.5000 W m^-2 K^-1
# OLR = A + B*T - F*ln(CO2/280 ppm), T in C: A = 210.00 W m^-2, B = 2.000 W m^-2 K^-1, F = 5.35 W m^-2
# Ice: linear transition of width 1.00 K centered on 0.00 C; an ice-covered band takes the ice albedo and the ice heat capacity (from the instantaneous temperature)
# Land fraction: 0.25 uniform (FILLET Table 4); one temperature per band (land and ocean blended in albedo and heat capacity)
# Convergence: converged after 20 orbits; max |T(t) - T(t - P)| over the final orbit = 5.80e-05 K (tolerance 1.0e-04 K)
# Hemispheric symmetry: max |T(lat) - T(-lat)| of the annual mean = 0.1298 K
#
# Columns of data (annually averaged for last orbit)
# Lat = latitude (deg); Tsurf = surface temperature (K); Asurf = surface albedo (unweighted time mean over the orbit); ATOA = top-of-atmosphere albedo (= Asurf, no atmospheric scattering); OLR = outgoing longwave radiation (W m^-2); Fland = land fraction of the band
